            <ArticleTitle>Modification of Selenoprotein mRNAs by Cap Tri-methylation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-141</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-4939-7258-6_9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Several selenoprotein mRNAs undergo 5' cap maturation events whereby their classical monomethylated m7G cap becomes trimethylated (m32,2,7G) by the trimethylguanosine synthase 1 (Tgs1). Here, we describe immunoprecipitation methods for the detection of endogenous m32,2,7G-capped selenoprotein mRNAs from total cell extracts or after polysome fractionation of cytoplasmic extracts. We have also developed a method for the in vitro cap hypermethylation of selenoprotein mRNA transcripts using purified Tgs1 enzyme.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
